<section class="hero compact">
    <p class="eyebrow">EMERALD / PACKAGE TOOLCHAIN</p>
    <h1>pkgbase</h1>

    <p class="lead">Build the base package metadata and filesystem database used by the Vylen package toolchain.</p>

    <div class="command-line"># pkgbase [options] &lt;package&gt;</div>

    <h2 id="help">
        <code>pkgbase help</code>
    </h2>

    <pre><code>Usage:
    pkgbase &lt;options&gt; [&lt;arg&gt;]

Options:
    -n, --dryrun  dry-run (show what would be removed without doing it)
    -y, --yes     don't ask user confirmation
    -h, --help    print this help message

Description:
    Removes all packages except base and specified packages.
    Keeps all dependencies of base and specified packages.

Examples:
    pkgbase -n vim git    # dry-run: show what would be removed
    pkgbase -y            # remove to base without confirmation
    pkgbase vim git curl  # keep vim, git, curl and their dependencies</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="doc">
    <h2 id="role">Role</h2>

    <p>
        <code>pkgbase</code> is a low-level package database utility used by the
        build and installation tools. It is not a replacement for Emerald
        transactions. Use it when inspecting or repairing package metadata in a
        controlled environment.
    </p>
</section>
